how do we draw a graph of a function y  or f of X equals 2x plus 1  y is equal to X plus 1 is the function  how do we represent this on a graph we  can easily manage to draw its graph  provided we know what a coordinate plane  is it is simply a surface on which we  can plot points lines and curves it just  makes life easy as it has the X and the  y axis now how do we plot this function  is the question to plot it all we have  to do is try substituting a few values  in place of X and get different values  for Y what will be the value of y if say  x is 0 0 plus 1 is 1 when x is 0 Y is 1  this point will be 0 comma 1 what if X  is 1 if X is 1 then Y will be 2 so 1  comma 2 here if X is 2 then Y will be 3  2 comma 3 honestly even two points are  enough to draw the line of this equation  but let's also try out a few negative  values of X if X is minus 1 then Y will  be minus 1 plus 1 0 minus 1 comma 0 will  be this point and if X is minus 2 then Y  will be minus 1 if we join all these  points what we get is a straight line so  this is the graph of this particular  equation it is a straight line because  it is a linear equation its degree is 1  what if the degree isn't 1 let's see  plot the graph of the function y is  equal to G of X is x squared  try drawing it on the XY axis  what will be the value of y if X is zero  square of zero is zero and hence Y will  also be zero the point will be zero  comma zero if X is 1 then Y will be 1  squared which is also 1 so 1 comma 1 if  X is 2 then Y will be 2 squared which is  4 2 comma 4 it's interesting it's  definitely not a straight line what is  it what if X is minus 1 Y will be the  square of minus 1 which is 1 this will  be the point minus 1 comma 1 if X is  minus 2 then Y will be the square of  minus 2 which is 4 minus 2 comma 4 is  the point joining all these points we  get a curve and it's called the parabola  plotting and understanding graphs of  functions is fun and it's also very  important for your exam prep we will  lo